          "role": "user",
          "content": "Compare surface codes and bosonic cat codes for fault-tolerant computing on small footprints.",
          "created_at": "2026-10-25T14:30:05Z"
        },
        {
          "id": "msg-1-2",
          "conversation_id": "demo-conv-1",
          "role": "assistant",
          "content": "Surface codes offer an established 2D layout with local 2-qubit stabilizers, but demand thousands of physical qubits per logical qubit.\n\nBosonic cat codes leverage infinite-dimensional Hilbert spaces in superconducting microwave cavities to autonomously correct bit flips via two-photon dissipation, leaving only phase flips for discrete outer layers. For a 6 GB local laptop workstation simulation, cat codes drastically reduce hardware state overhead.",
